{"name":"Toasted Coconut","hex":"#e9c2a1","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"toasted","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cooked by toasting.","Very hot."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of toast"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toasted"},{"term":"coconut","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fruit of the coconut palm (not a true nut), Cocos nucifera, having a fibrous husk surrounding a large seed.","A hard-shelled seed of this fruit, having white flesh and a fluid-filled central cavity."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coconut"}],"entries":[{"title":"Toast (food)","blocks":[{"text":"Toast is sliced bread that has been browned by radiant heat. The browning is the result of a Maillard reaction altering the flavor of the bread and making it crispier in texture. The firm surface is easier to spread toppings on and the warmth can help spreads such as butter reach their melting point. Toasting is a common method of making stale bread more palatable. Bread is commonly toasted using devices specifically designed for such, e.g., a toaster or a toaster oven. Toast may contain more acrylamide, caused by the browning process, which is suspected to be a carcinogen. However, claims that acrylamide in burnt food causes cancer have not been proven."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Toast-3.jpg/330px-Toast-3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toast_(food)"},{"title":"Coconut","blocks":[{"text":"The coconut is a member of the palm family (Arecaceae) and the only living species of the genus Cocos. The term \"coconut\" can denote the whole coconut palm tree or the large hard fruit. Originally native to the Southeast Asia, New Guinea, and the Southwestern Pacific, they are ubiquitous in coastal tropical regions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Cocos_nucifera_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-187.jpg/330px-Cocos_nucifera_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-187.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coconut"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Toaster.jpg/500px-Toaster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Toaster.jpg/1280px-Toaster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Toaster.jpg/500px-Toaster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A classic two-slot toaster","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AToaster.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Vegemite_and_jelly.jpg/500px-Vegemite_and_jelly.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Vegemite_and_jelly.jpg/1280px-Vegemite_and_jelly.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Vegemite_and_jelly.jpg/500px-Vegemite_and_jelly.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Left: Toast with butter and Vegemite. Right: With butter and strawberry jam.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVegemite_and_jelly.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Toasts_photographed_in_West_Bengal%2C_India.jpg/500px-Toasts_photographed_in_West_Bengal%2C_India.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Toasts_photographed_in_West_Bengal%2C_India.jpg/1280px-Toasts_photographed_in_West_Bengal%2C_India.jpg?